{"number": 248, "text": "            Appendix       7    Phrasal    verbs    + object                                                    |\n            (put   out   A fire  / try  on   clothes,    etc.)                                                  |\n\n\n           This is a list of some important phrasal verbs + object (see Unit 113).\n\n                       fill out a form = complete a form\n\n                          ©   Can you fill out this form, please?\n                       put out a fire, a cigarette, etc.\n                              The fire department arrived and put the fire out.                FILL OUT\n                       cross out a mistake, a word, etc.\n                         ©    If you make a mistake, cross it out.\n                                                                 PUT OUT\n                                                                                          CROSS OUT\n\n                       try on clothes = put on clothes to see if they fit you\n                         ©    (ina store) Where can | try these pants on?\n                       give up something = stop doing / having something\n                         (©   Sue gave up her job when her baby was born. (= she stopped working)\n                         ©    Tom's doctor told him he had to give up smoking.\n                       look up a word in a dictionary, etc.\n                         (©)  I didn’t know the meaning of the word, so | looked it up in a dictionary.\n                       turn up the TV, radio, music, heat, etc. = make it louder or warmer\n                         ()   Can you turn the radio up? | can't hear it.\n                       wake up somebody  who  is sleeping\n                              | have to get up early tomorrow. Can you wake me up at 6:30?\n                       tear down A building = demolish it                 TEAR  Y  =\n                         ©   They are going to tear down the school\n                              and build a new one.\n                       turn down  the TV. radio. music hear ere\n                       = make it      or less warm\n                         ©    The music is too loud. Can you turn it down?\n\n                       knock over a cup, a glass, a person, etc.\n\n                         ©    Be careful. Don’t knock your cup over.                 :\n                                                                          KNOCK OVER\n\n                       throw away garbage, things you don’t want\n                         (©  These apples are bad. Should | throw them away?\n                                                                                THROW AWAY\n                         ©    Don’t throw away that picture. | want it.                   ae\n                       put something away = put it in the place where you usually keep it of =    :\n                         ©)  After they finished playing, the children put their toys away.\n                       pay somebody  back = give back money that you borrowed\n                              Thank you for lending me the money. pay you back next week.\n                       show somebody  around  = take somebody on a tour of a place\n                         ()  We  visited a factory last week. The manager showed us around.\n\n\n                                                                                                        237", "char_count": 3381, "mean_conf": 88.71, "word_count": 407, "words": [{"text": "This", "x0": 253, "y0": 311, "x1": 327, "y1": 347, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "is", "x0": 343, "y0": 313, "x1": 366, "y1": 347, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "a", "x0": 379, "y0": 323, "x1": 398, "y1": 347, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "list", "x0": 413, "y0": 311, "x1": 463, "y1": 347, "conf": 94, "bold": false}, {"text": "of", "x0": 476, "y0": 311, "x1": 517, "y1": 347, "conf": 89, "bold": false}, {"text": "some", "x0": 527, "y0":